Emacsvox for Debian and Ubuntu
=============================

Install a downloaded package with apt, which resolves its Emacs dependency:

  sudo apt install ./emacsvox_VERSION_all.deb

Emacs 30.2 or newer is required. Settings menus need elpa-transient 0.13.3
or newer, or Emacs 31.1 or newer with a supported bundled Transient.
Ubuntu 26.10 supplies these dependencies. Ubuntu 26.04's stock Transient is
too old; use the source-install route with an Emacs package-manager upgrade.
Omnivox 1.18.0 or newer is recommended.
If Omnivox is not in your configured apt repositories, install its downloaded
deb in the same apt command, or supply an existing Omnivox installation.
The package does not add repositories, download engines or build GNU Emacs.
An Emacs built outside dpkg does not satisfy the package dependency: use the
source installer if you want to rely exclusively on a per-user Emacs build.

Start an isolated session with:

  emacsvox --diagnose
  emacsvox --check
  emacsvox

Confirm that --check produces both tone and speech before ordinary use.
Use emacsvox -nw for a terminal session. EMACS selects another supported
executable. OMNIVOX_PROGRAM and the existing per-user Omnivox configuration
select the speech executable; installing this package does not change them.

For remote Emacs or WSL using an existing Windows Omnivox, omit the local
Linux speech engine with:

  sudo apt install --no-install-recommends ./emacsvox_VERSION_all.deb

For remote speech, use emacsvox --remote --diagnose and then emacsvox --remote
after preparing the workstation service, private token and SSH reverse tunnel.
Use Omnivox 1.18.0 or newer; Emacsvox remote access remains a preview
feature. For WSL desktop speech, select the native
Windows omnivox.exe with OMNIVOX_PROGRAM or your existing per-user setting.
The guided WSL source installer remains the route for acquiring that runtime.

Files live under /usr/share/emacsvox; the public command is /usr/bin/emacsvox.
The manual is /usr/share/emacsvox/info/emacsvox.info (also available from
Emacsvox help). To enable speech in your personal Emacs, explicitly add:

  (load-file "/usr/share/emacsvox/lisp/emacsvox-setup.el")

No site startup file is installed and no personal initialization is edited.
The package loads Lisp sources; no .elc files are shipped or generated
at installation time. Optional integrations need their corresponding tools
or Emacs packages; Hydra convenience menus need the hydra Emacs package.
Source-checkout build and guided installation commands do not apply to this
read-only system tree. Upgrade it using apt. Removal leaves personal settings,
speech tokens and logs intact.

BUILD-INFO.json records source identity and the autoload generation toolchain.
Versions containing +git and -0local1 are local development builds, not
published releases.
